xanthoproteic.en:
a. Pertaining to, or derived from, xanthoprotein;
   showing the characters of xanthoprotein; as, xanthoproteic acid; the
   xanthoproteic reaction for albumin.

xylic.en:
a. Pertaining to, derived from, or related to, xylene;
   specifically, designating any one of several metameric acids produced
   by the partial oxidation of mesitylene and pseudo-cumene.

xylylene.en:
n. Any one of three metameric radicals, CH2.C6H4.CH2,
   derived respectively from the three xylenes. Often used adjectively;
   as, xylylene alcohol.
